Everything under this directory comes from Movement Range Maps, published
by AI for Good at Meta (formerly Data for Good at Meta) on the Humanitarian
Data Exchange:

  https://data.humdata.org/dataset/movement-range-maps

HDX lists the dataset's licence as Creative Commons Attribution International
(CC BY, license_id cc-by); it is used here as CC BY 4.0.

Credit:

  Data for Good at Meta, Movement Range Maps, Humanitarian Data Exchange
  (https://data.humdata.org/dataset/movement-range-maps)

The files under movement-range-maps/original/ are Meta's own, byte for
byte; manifest.json records each one's size, sha256 and dates.

The Parquet under movement-range-maps/ was made from them:

  - the tab separated file inside each zip was read and split into one table
    a year (2020, 2021, 2022)
  - ds became a date and the two measures doubles; the other columns are the
    text of the files
  - a source_file column was added, naming the file each row came from
  - rows were sorted by country, region and day
  - values were not changed

The code that fetches, checks and converts is MIT, in the repository this
dataset was built from (https://github.com/yuiseki/meta-range-maps-2022-05), and does
not apply here.
